      "text": "The decimal representation of the number 1/7 is 0.\\overline{142857}. This means that the decimal repeats every six digits: 142857, 142857, 142857, 142857, 142857, and 142857.\n\nTo find the 100th digit after the decimal point, we need to determine the position of the digit in the repeating sequence. We can do this by finding the remainder when 100 is divided by 6 (the length of the repeating sequence).\n\n100 ÷ 6 = 16 remainder 4\n\nThis means that the 100th digit is the same as the 4th digit in the repeating sequence, which is 2.\n\nTherefore, the 100th digit after the decimal point of the decimal representation of 1/7 is \\boxed{2}.",
