    {
      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "To find the decimal representation of \\( \\frac{1}{7} \\), we perform the division \\( 1 \\div 7 \\):\n\n\\[\n1 \\div 7 = 0.\\overline{142857}\n\\]\n\nThe decimal representation of \\( \\frac{1}{7} \\) is \\( 0.142857142857\\ldots \\), which means the digits \"142857\" repeat indefinitely. The cycle length of the repeating block is 6 digits.\n\nTo determine the 100th digit after the decimal point, we need to find the position of the 100th digit within the repeating cycle. We do this by calculating the remainder when 100 is divided by 6:\n\n\\[\n100 \\div 6 = 16 \\text{ remainder } 4\n\\]\n\nThe remainder is 4, which means that the 100th digit corresponds to the 4th digit in the repeating block \"142857\". Looking at the block \"142857\", we see that the 4th digit is 2.\n\nTherefore, the 100th digit after the decimal point of the decimal representation of \\( \\frac{1}{7} \\) is \\(\\boxed{2}\\).",
