    {
      "sample_index": 2,
      "text": "To determine the 100th digit after the decimal point of the decimal representation of \\( \\frac{1}{7} \\), we first need to find the decimal representation of \\( \\frac{1}{7} \\).\n\nPerforming the division \\( 1 \\div 7 \\), we get:\n\\[\n\\frac{1}{7} = 0.\\overline{142857}\n\\]\nThis means that the decimal representation of \\( \\frac{1}{7} \\) is a repeating decimal with the repeating block \"142857\". The length of this repeating block is 6 digits.\n\nTo find the 100th digit after the decimal point, we need to determine the position of the 100th digit within the repeating block. We do this by finding the remainder when 100 is divided by 6:\n\\[\n100 \\div 6 = 16 \\text{ remainder } 4\n\\]\nThis tells us that the 100th digit corresponds to the 4th digit in the repeating block \"142857\". The digits in the repeating block are: 1, 4, 2, 8, 5, 7. Therefore, the 4th digit is 2.\n\nThus, the 100th digit after the decimal point of the decimal representation of \\( \\frac{1}{7} \\) is \\(\\boxed{2}\\).",
